                "entry_id": "50e1796d-e380-3d32-8509-1b5d1f868ed3",
                "word": "noddle",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f827292a-c257-436b-a78c-38ead188abe6",
                        "entry_id": "50e1796d-e380-3d32-8509-1b5d1f868ed3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "noddles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "07b9d971-b409-3b4e-a63d-6cc6603db68a",
                        "entry_id": "50e1796d-e380-3d32-8509-1b5d1f868ed3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The head; the part of the body of an animal or human which contains the brain, mouth and main sense organs."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "64f657c4-8955-4e7e-a813-415b7585209b",
                                "sense_id": "07b9d971-b409-3b4e-a63d-6cc6603db68a",
                                "text": "But being restored to the open aire, the cafe with him was little altred; for no roofe had he to hide his noddle in, or whither he might go to set up his rest, but in the streets under a bulk he should have been constrainted to have kenneld […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3fe07555-e6ab-35a5-b7e1-9fe80d72a2d5",
                        "entry_id": "50e1796d-e380-3d32-8509-1b5d1f868ed3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The head as the seat of mental capacity or intellect."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5819e3f7-cf7b-4d4c-b762-8ab97ca28bd1",
                                "sense_id": "3fe07555-e6ab-35a5-b7e1-9fe80d72a2d5",
                                "text": "No doubt (said the Barber) but I wonder not so much at the Knights madnesse, as the Squires simplicity, that beleeves so in the Islands, and I think all the Art in the world will not drive that out of his noddle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6837fe1a-0c6c-407a-8e77-f477b39b0788",
                                "sense_id": "3fe07555-e6ab-35a5-b7e1-9fe80d72a2d5",
                                "text": "Thus far the Poet; but his brains grow Addle, / And all the reſt is purely from this Noddle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "413af343-1380-4412-afcd-a46ae75a0166",
                                "sense_id": "3fe07555-e6ab-35a5-b7e1-9fe80d72a2d5",
                                "text": "Novv vvhat can have got into that precious noddle of thine, my dear brother Toby? cried my father, mentally."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "358134e6-3367-3733-915c-6a52fd72ca83",
                        "entry_id": "50e1796d-e380-3d32-8509-1b5d1f868ed3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The back of the head; nape."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8fd8e720-c034-41c1-8f4f-4873ff05ded9",
                                "sense_id": "358134e6-3367-3733-915c-6a52fd72ca83",
                                "text": "They muste absteine from ouer much slepe, and not to slepe in the day time, nor [upon] the noddle of the head […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
